WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.510
So Perry and I have been running
the executive programs at the D School

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.220
at Stanford for the last several year.

3
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.350
And we've had the great pleasure
of hosting hundreds and

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.590
thousands of professionals,

5
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.730
just like you, at Stanford, getting them
immersed in the tools of design thinking.

6
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.480
But we weren't satisfied just
with hosting professionals here.

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.280
Our goal with Innovation at Work is to
take the same tools that we teach here at

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.020
Stanford and
bring them in to your context.

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.160
In to your office and put them to work
on challenges that matter to you.

10
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.830
&gt;&gt; So
how it is going to work is each portion

11
00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.700
of Innovation at Work has two sections.

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.850
One is about actually practicing a skill
and the other is doing it at work.

13
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.740
The way it's gonna work is we will
give an instructional video, and

14
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.470
there are injections even throughout that
that'll run concurrent with your work.

15
00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.640
So you'll be working
sometimes right beside us.

16
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.820
Sometimes we'll prompt you to do work,
and you'll dive right into it.

17
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.000
Whatever it is, though, I assure you
it's gonna be active in the room.

18
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.730
You're gonna be up,
you're gonna be moving, and

19
00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.098
you're gonna be using
these tools real time.

20
00:01:00.098 --> 00:01:02.790
&gt;&gt; This Innovation at Work
course is different from

21
00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.050
any other online course you've taken.

22
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.450
For two reasons.

23
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.620
One, it's actually project based, meaning,
that we'll give some instruction and

24
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.990
then you're working on a real project.

25
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.860
The second thing is, rather than sitting
with your own computer at your desk,

26
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.920
doing the class by yourself,
you'll be with a group of your colleagues,

27
00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.300
working on developing these tools and
applying them to your challenge together.

28
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.710
So people who generally come to Innovation
at Work, leave their laptops at their

29
00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.880
desk, and come with an attitude ready to
engage and collaborate and an openness

30
00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:38.810
to try on new tools of innovation to
bring back to their team and their work.

31
00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.240
&gt;&gt; So these Innovation at Work sessions
will each be about 90 minutes.

32
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.040
The first one will always be practice,
we'll actually go through a skill and

33
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.280
actually sort of tool you up and
actually use a challenge that we have to

34
00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.650
teach you the tools that
we want you to learn.

35
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:56.430
The second one will always be about
a problem that you have in your work and

36
00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.639
we'll apply those tools to that challenge.

37
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.605
In the sessions, we'll give instruction
and videos sometimes demonstrating.

38
00:02:03.605 --> 00:02:06.055
We'll give a certain amount
of time to get it done but

39
00:02:06.055 --> 00:02:09.420
know that if you need to hit play or
pause during the session.

40
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:16.695
&gt;&gt; That's pretty cool.

41
00:02:16.695 --> 00:02:21.910
[LAUGH] You can do that and you can
actually continue on with the session

42
00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.500
as if we were there the whole time.

43
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.030
&gt;&gt; Right.
&gt;&gt; The goal though is for

44
00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:29.150
you to take these tools seriously and
for you to feel confident and

45
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.660
capable of applying them to
work that matters to you.

46
00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.740
&gt;&gt; Yeah and one more thing I forgot
to tell you, the sessions are active.

47
00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.120
&gt;&gt; You won't need a computer at all.

48
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:38.755
&gt;&gt; That's great.

49
00:02:38.755 --> 00:02:41.584
[SOUND]

